# 30. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The project is complete only when these workflows work end to end.

1. A user can create an account and join an organization.
2. An organization admin can invite members and assign roles.
3. An authorized user can create a workspace.
4. An authorized user can upload a supported document.
5. The file is stored privately and indexed asynchronously.
6. The UI shows actual indexing progress and failures.
7. An authorized user can ask a question about the indexed document.
8. The AI produces a grounded answer with valid source citations.
9. A citation opens the correct authorized document and page.
10. An unsupported question produces an honest no-evidence response.
11. A user cannot retrieve another organization's documents or conversations.
12. A user cannot retrieve documents from an unauthorized department or workspace.
13. Revoking access prevents future retrieval and citation access.
14. Deleted documents disappear from search and RAG retrieval.
15. Administrators can inspect real usage, latency, processing failures, and estimated AI costs.
16. Feedback and audit events persist correctly.
17. The application handles provider errors and queue failures gracefully.
18. Security tests verify the critical authorization boundaries.
19. The application can be run locally using the documented setup.
20. Production build, type checks, and required tests pass.

Do not mark an acceptance criterion complete based solely on a UI screenshot.

